{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Const-Correct Clustering Operation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Const-Correct Clustering Operation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"const correct clustering operation const correct clustering operation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Const-Correct Clustering Operation.md","fileName":"Const-Correct Clustering Operation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Const-Correct Clustering Operation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 22:06\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[C++ Clustering Object Model]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Clustering Object Model","dataclusteringincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Const-Correct Clustering Operation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Const-Correct Clustering Operation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"const correct clustering operation const correct clustering operation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Const-Correct Clustering Operation.md","fileName":"Const-Correct Clustering Operation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Const-Correct Clustering Operation","heading":"Const-Correct Clustering Operation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Const-correctness distinguishes operations that may change an object's logical configuration from those that only observe it. Clustering accessors return const references when clients should inspect a schema or result without replacing it, and computational hooks can be const when parameters must remain fixed.\n\nThe compiler then prevents accidental mutation across the interface. Working outputs that legitimately change during a const computation must be isolated explicitly rather than weakening const guarantees for the entire algorithm.","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Clustering Object Model","dataclusteringincplusplus